# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# scripts/figures.db — ONE GENERIC DECLARATION FOR EVERY PINNED NUMBER
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ⛔ THIS IS NOT A CLONE-METER FEATURE. A "figure" is any pinned number a
# guard, a report or a reader depends on: a ratchet ceiling, a parity floor, an
# exact meter pin, a policy budget, a benchmark, a census. The clone meters are
# the PILOT because they are the hard case (exact-pin + a declared non-zero
# input + a per-round authorization band); a schema that expresses them
# expresses a leak ceiling or a coverage floor trivially.
#
# THE GENERALISING AXIS IS POLARITY, NOT SUBJECT. Subject ("clone", "parity",
# "fmt") is a naming convention and carries zero behaviour.
#
#   polarity      what a checker DOES with the number
#     shrink-only   measured <= value   a ratchet: may fall, never rise
#     grow-only     measured >= value   a floor:   may rise, never fall
#     exact-pin     measured == value   (± band_pct against band_anchor)
#     informational NEVER RED           a report; a table, not a gate
#
#   provenance    where `value` CAME FROM — an ORTHOGONAL axis
#     measured      an instrument ran and printed it; `regen` observes BEHAVIOUR
#     derived       copied/computed from a declared `authority`; `regen` READS
#                   a declaration instead of measuring
#     policy        CHOSEN. `regen = none` is legal ONLY here, and `authority`
#                   is mandatory: who chose it, and where the choice is recorded
#
#   ⚠ THE DISCRIMINATOR between `measured` and `derived`, stated once: does the
#     regen OBSERVE BEHAVIOUR (run a test, run a binary, count files) or READ A
#     DECLARATION (grep a constant, copy another row)? Observe ⇒ measured. Read
#     ⇒ derived, and then `authority` names what is read.
#
#   ⛔ `policy` IS NOT A FIFTH POLARITY — AND THE PROOF IS NOT "IT CROSSES MORE
#     THAN ONE POLARITY". It does not: `policy` occupies exactly ONE cell here
#     (shrink-only), because the row that would have given it a second,
#     `SHAPE_MAX_DEPTH`, is correctly ruled NEVER. An earlier revision of this
#     paragraph made the crossing claim anyway; it was false the moment that
#     ruling stood, and it is exactly the "class statement reached by
#     resemblance" this file's own doctrine warns about.
#     THE TRUE PROOF IS THAT NEITHER AXIS IS A FUNCTION OF THE OTHER:
#       polarity does NOT determine provenance — `exact-pin` carries both
#         `measured` (the clone pins) and `derived` (`fmt.max_width`), and
#         `shrink-only` carries both `measured` (`proc_guard.no_deadline_
#         baseline`) and `policy` (`agents_md.size_ceiling`);
#       provenance does NOT determine polarity — `measured` carries `exact-pin`,
#         `grow-only`, `shrink-only` AND `informational`.
#     Two independent questions about one row, and `tests/lints.rs::
#     figures_db_axes_are_occupied` fails if either fact stops holding.
#
# ── THE VALUE IS THE GUARD, NOT THIS FILE ──────────────────────────────────
# A figures file with no lint forbidding an undeclared bare literal of a
# covered figure is a sixth spelling with better manners. The enforcement:
#   tests/lints.rs::figures_db_rows_are_wellformed          the schema contract
#   tests/lints.rs::figures_db_mirrors_agree                MIRROR-mode drift
#   tests/lints.rs::figures_db_values_have_one_spelling     the uniqueness guard
#   tests/lints.rs::figures_db_scanner_sees_into_doc_comments  it catches its own
#   python3 scripts/figures.py --validate | --scan | --census | check <row>
#
# ── ADOPTION IS MIRROR-MODE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The literal STAYS in the code; the row declares where, and
# `figures_db_mirrors_agree` REDs when the two drift. The alternative (SOURCED:
# delete the literal, have the consumer read the row) is deliberately NOT used
# here — sourcing the clone pins would delete the very literals
# `clone_meter_pins_carry_their_provenance` reads, and it delivers nothing the
# uniqueness guard does not already deliver.
#
# ── FORMAT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXACTLY `scripts/clone_meter.spec`'s restricted dialect, and for its reason:
# `key = value`, one per line, WHOLE-LINE `#` comments only, no trailing
# whitespace on any line, blank lines ignored, a repeated key is a list.
# ⛔ NOT TOML — one reader is awk (`scripts/figures.sh`), and awk strips only a
# leading whitespace run while Rust `trim()`s both ends, so a trailing space
# would reach a shell reader intact.
# ⚠ KEYS ARE DOTTED, AND EVERY READER COMPARES THEM AS WHOLE STRINGS. The
# precedent's `clone_meter_get` matches its key as a REGEX, where `.` is a
# wildcard — `figures_get` in scripts/figures.sh uses an exact `==` instead.
#
# ── FIELDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MANDATORY on every row:
#   value          the figure, bare digits (separators are normalised anyway)
#   unit           what it counts
#   polarity       shrink-only | grow-only | exact-pin | informational
#   provenance     measured | derived | policy
#   regen          the command that reproduces a number to compare against;
#                  `none` ONLY under provenance = policy
#   regen_extract  a regex with a NAMED `(?P<value>...)` capture. ⛔ MANDATORY,
#                  NO DEFAULT — "the last integer in stdout" is a silent lie:
#                  it yields 0 for c_emit_comparison and 1 for
#                  resolver_comparison, not 1283 and 1865
#   regen_fires    a regex whose match COUNT proves the mechanism executed
#   regen_env      NAME=value / NAME=unset pairs the regen must run under, or
#                  `none`. ⚠ This is the real hazard: `GG_BACKEND=llvm` makes
#                  `parity_floor_active` return false and captures a DIFFERENT,
#                  unseeded count under the very same regex
#   instrument     the tool that produces the number
#   measured_at    the commit the recorded value was taken at
#   home           where a reader should look for the figure
#   scan           `standard` (the declared roots below) | `none` | paths
#   caveat         what the figure does NOT mean; `none` is a claim, not a gap
#   cost_secs      the DEADLINE `figures.py` hands `proc_guard.run`, seeded
#                  from the measured cost of `regen` and rounded generously UP —
#                  a deadline equal to the measured time is a flake. Or
#                  `unmeasured`, and then `check` REFUSES to run the row without
#                  an explicit `--timeout`: a spawn with no chosen deadline is
#                  the class `scripts/proc_guard.py` exists to retire
# CONDITIONAL:
#   authority      mandatory for provenance derived AND policy; forbidden for
#                  measured (its authority is the instrument)
#   input          mandatory; `none`, or a named input that also owes
#                  input.<name>.at / .law / .regen
#                  ⚠ `input = none` means NO QUANTIFIED INPUT, not "nothing can
#                  move this". A suspected-but-unmeasured axis belongs in
#                  `caveat`, which is exactly how `scripts/clone_meter.spec`
#                  splits its MEASURED-to-be-zero table from the rows nobody has
#                  varied. An input with a law you have not measured is a rumour
#                  promoted to a field, and it would poison the field for the
#                  rows that did the work
# OPTIONAL:
#   mirror         `<path>:<symbol>` — a declared literal that must EQUAL value
#   waiver         `<path> <count> declared|debt <reason>` — the EXACT number of
#                  unmasked spellings expected in that file. ⚠ EXACT, not `<=`:
#                  a STALE waiver must be as red as a new duplicate, or the
#                  guard waivers itself into uselessness
#   band_pct       + band_anchor: an exact-pin's authorization band, anchored on
#                  another ROW (a pointer, never a second copy of a number)
#   regen_forbids  a regex that must NOT appear (a skip notice)
#   note           anything else worth pinning to the row
#
# ── SCAN ROOTS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⛔ `docs/define-gorget/decisions.md` is NOT a scan root and never becomes one.
# A dated measurement inside a ratified entry is EVIDENCE FOR THE RULING AT THE
# TIME IT WAS MADE; a guard that forced it to point at a live value would change
# what the entry asserts. The ledger records what was measured THEN; this file
# records what is true NOW. Same reason for `DONE.md`: a round record is history.
figures.scan_roots = tests/integration.rs tests/lints.rs todo docs/devbook TODO.md scripts
figures.scan_skip = scripts/figures.db
#
# ⛔ WHAT THE SCANNER CANNOT SEE — SAY THE REACH, NEVER IMPLY TOTALITY. A guard
# that is read as total is worse than one whose limits are written down (the
# lesson `todo/t0875` was filed for). Probe-verified at the time of writing:
#   * `src/` — NOT a root. 11 files there carry integer const declarations. A
#     row whose `home`/`mirror` is in `src/` IS scanned (a declared path is
#     always opened), but an UNDECLARED re-spelling in `src/` is invisible.
#   * `tests/*.rs` other than `integration.rs` and `lints.rs` — invisible.
#     `tests/spec_conformance.rs` alone carries 4 integer const declarations.
#   * `docs/` outside `docs/devbook/` — `book/`, `internals/`, `census/`,
#     `profiling/`, `language-reference.md` are all unscanned.
#   * THE EXTENSION FILTER: only `.md .rs .py .sh .spec .toml` are opened.
#     `.gg` fixtures, `.json` baselines, `.tsv` manifests and `Makefile`-shaped
#     files inside the roots are invisible even though their directory is a root.
#   * `DONE.md` and `docs/define-gorget/` are excluded ON PURPOSE (above), not
#     by oversight.
# ⇒ Widening a root is cheap and is the right move when a family of rows lands
#   there; widening it BLINDLY is not — every new file is new waiver surface.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE PILOT — the clone meters (exact-pin × measured, with a declared input)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Eight constants, four axes, two roles. The PIN moves at every integration; the
# ROUND-OPEN anchor moves once, at round open, and is what the ~1% authorization
# band is evaluated against. They start each round equal and legitimately
# diverge inside it, which is why they are eight ROWS and not four: a single row
# mirroring both would RED on a legitimate intra-round re-pin.
row = clone.self_compile.array.pin
row = clone.self_compile.array.round_open
row = clone.self_compile.string.pin
row = clone.self_compile.string.round_open
row = clone.stage1.array.pin
row = clone.stage1.array.round_open
row = clone.stage1.string.pin
row = clone.stage1.string.round_open

clone.self_compile.array.pin.value = 13150071
clone.self_compile.array.pin.unit = array_clone calls, stage-0 self-compile
clone.self_compile.array.pin.polarity = exact-pin
clone.self_compile.array.pin.provenance = measured
clone.self_compile.array.pin.regen = cargo test --test integration --release self_host_clone_ceiling -- --nocapture
clone.self_compile.array.pin.regen_extract = \[clone-ceiling\] array_clone=(?P<value>[0-9_,]+)
clone.self_compile.array.pin.regen_fires = \[clone-ceiling\] [a-z_]+=[0-9]+ .*verdict=
clone.self_compile.array.pin.regen_env = GG_BACKEND=unset
clone.self_compile.array.pin.instrument = tests/integration.rs::self_host_clone_ceiling
clone.self_compile.array.pin.measured_at = 4c473a88
clone.self_compile.array.pin.home = tests/integration.rs:SELF_COMPILE_ARRAY_CLONE_PIN
clone.self_compile.array.pin.scan = standard
clone.self_compile.array.pin.caveat = C backend only — --clones=stats is rejected under --backend=llvm, so an LLVM-only clone regression rides under this pin (todo/t0550)
clone.self_compile.array.pin.cost_secs = 1800
clone.self_compile.array.pin.mirror = tests/integration.rs:SELF_COMPILE_ARRAY_CLONE_PIN
clone.self_compile.array.pin.band_pct = 1
clone.self_compile.array.pin.band_anchor = clone.self_compile.array.round_open
clone.self_compile.array.pin.waiver = tests/integration.rs 2 declared the PINNED-BY / ROUND-OPENED-BY provenance lines, which clone_meter_pins_carry_their_provenance requires to BIND the value
clone.self_compile.array.pin.input = none
clone.self_compile.array.pin.note = the array axis is checkout-invariant; only the string axis carries the root-path input

clone.self_compile.array.round_open.value = 13150071
